<http://data.silknow.org/object/e08e13f7-596b-3fb6-bc29-567fd7c7a921/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Although it does not contain metal thread, the complex weave of this velvet imitates the effects of a richly looped cloth of gold. It would not have been as expensive as real cloth of gold, but would still have been a fabric of high status. \nThe velvet was acquired by the Museum as part of a dalmatic, a type of sleeved tunic worn by some clergy in the Christian Church."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e08e13f7-596b-3fb6-bc29-567fd7c7a921> .

